# Review settings help texts (organiser-facing, but they describe the
# reviewers' workflow, so the vocabulary has to match).
#: pretalx/submission/interfaces/forms/review.py
msgid ""
"Please give a fair review on why you’d like to see this proposal at the "
"conference, or why you think it would not be a good fit."
msgstr ""
"Please give a fair assessment of this application: what speaks for the "
"candidate, and what gives you pause."

#: pretalx/orga/forms/review.py
msgid ""
"If you select “all”, reviewers can review all proposals that their teams "
"have access to (so either all, or specific tracks). In this mode, assigned "
"proposals will be highlighted and will be shown first in the review "
"workflow. "
msgstr ""
"If you select “all”, reviewers can review every application their team has "
"access to. Applications assigned to them are highlighted and shown first."

#: pretalx/orga/forms/review.py
msgid ""
"By default, modification of proposals is locked after the CfP ends, and is "
"re-enabled once the proposal was accepted."
msgstr ""
"By default, applicants can no longer edit their application once the "
"deadline has passed."

#: pretalx/orga/templates/orga/settings/review.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"If you require neither a review score nor a review text, reviewers will be "
"offered an additional %(quotation_open)sAbstain%(quotation_close)s button "
"when reviewing proposals."
msgstr ""
"If you require neither a review score nor a review text, reviewers get an "
"extra %(quotation_open)sAbstain%(quotation_close)s button when reviewing "
"applications."

#: pretalx/orga/templates/orga/event/dashboard.html
msgid ""
"Your event will no longer be publicly visible: the schedule, session and "
"speaker pages will only be accessible to you and your team."
msgstr ""
"This page will no longer be publicly visible: applicants will not be able to"
" reach the application form or their own application."

